WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.310
The hilarious and critically-acclaimed Mitchells
vs The Machines is so positively bursting

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.200
with easter eggs, in-jokes, and film references
that you might wear out your pause button

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.679
trying to spot them all.

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:15.910
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing over one hundred

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.950
crazy details and secrets hidden in The Mitchells
vs The Machines.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.180
Some spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:27.140
The movie kicks off with a cell phone being
crushed beneath the foot of a PAL robot, referencing

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.180
the famous scene from the 90s robot apocalypse
movie Terminator 2: Judgment Day of a skull

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.950
being crushed underfoot by a killer bot.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:39.440
PAL, the name of the operating system and
digital personal assistant who orchestrates

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.280
the robo-pocalypse after being tossed aside
by her human creator, is a reference to HAL

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:50.300
9000, the AI antagonist from Stanley Kubrick's
epic sci-fi 2001: A Space Odyssey,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.880
who also turned against his human operators
when he discovered they planned to disconnect

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:55.880
him.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.820
The red dot on each of the PAL robots' heads
is also a nod to HAL's depiction as a camera

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.060
lens with a red dot in the middle.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:06.909
And at the Dino Stop, when Katie orders the
two PAL robots not to take them, the dot on

00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:12.100
their head changes from red to blue to subtly
signal their change in character from antagonists

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.060
to the more helpful bots they turn out to
be.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:20.640
PAL also has the feel of the mega tech company
Apple, and the shiny PAL retail store the

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.350
Mitchells visit in the mall has Apple Store
vibes.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:28.680
And coincidentally, or not, if you rearrange
the letters in PAL to A-P-L, it very much

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.520
sounds like Apple!

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.780
When PAL is revealed to her creator Mark as
the villain at the heart of the robot conspiracy,

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.670
the evil cell phone swivels round on her chair,
like a Bond villain, and you can see she's

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.070
sitting on a small pile of books.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:45.670
The top one is "The Master Algorithm" which
examines machine learning and predicts the

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:49.850
rise of a "master algorithm" that will come
to a perfect understanding of the world and

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:50.850
humanity.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:54.909
In the middle is "The Art of War", the ancient
treatise that has influenced both military

00:01:54.909 --> 00:01:57.580
and business strategy and tactics across the
world.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:01.439
And the book at the base of the pile is titled
"The Singularity Is Near",

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:05.320
another real-life book whose author predicts
that machine intelligence will eventually

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.219
surpass human intelligence and bring about
a technological singularity, an event which

00:02:10.219 --> 00:02:11.920
comes to pass in The Mitchells movie.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:18.239
The look of the movie's sleek white robots
draws on Honda's humanoid robot ASIMO, which

00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:23.189
was created in the year 2000 and named after
sci-fi writer Isaac Asimov,

00:02:23.189 --> 00:02:27.819
which is especially fitting because the scenes
of marching robot armies remind me of both

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:32.760
the movie I, Robot, starring Will Smith, and
the Stormtroopers from Star Wars.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.079
By the way, the filmmakers have said the robots
use a "fully developed robot language" which

00:02:37.079 --> 00:02:39.799
contains secret jokes for anyone who can crack
it.

00:02:39.799 --> 00:02:41.799
You can see the robots using it as they type.

00:02:41.799 --> 00:02:45.810
To figure out the code, look closely at the
scenes of the robots taking over different

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:50.069
cities around the world and you can see how
each city's name is translated into the robot

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.409
language.

00:02:51.409 --> 00:02:54.730
One of the best moments in the movie comes
when the Mitchells are attacked by a mass

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.969
of PAL-chipped machines and take cover in
a toy store,

00:02:57.969 --> 00:03:04.069
only then to be confronted by a horrifying
army of Furbies who begin to talk in their

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:06.209
own language.

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:12.659
This Furby form of communication is referencing
the original Furby toys who when newly purchased

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:17.329
spoke a language called Furbish and were programmed
to only begin to speak English gradually each

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:18.860
time they were turned on.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:23.559
In The Mitchells, the Furbies' vocalizations
are suitably horrifying, hilarious and creepy

00:03:23.559 --> 00:03:29.389
at the same time.

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:38.319
The Mitchells' dog Monchi, with his ability
to make the robots error and explode, turns

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:40.870
out to be one of the MVPs of the movie.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.290
"Dog shield, activate!"

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:43.290
"Dog?

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.290
Dog?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.290
Dog?

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.290
Loaf of bread.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.290
System error.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:50.590
[spluttering] Dog-- Pig-- Bread-- Loaf--"
Celebrity dog Doug the Pug, who has millions

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:55.139
of followers online, provided Monchi's barks,
grunts, sneezes, snores, licks, and other

00:03:55.139 --> 00:03:57.019
assorted canine noises.

00:03:57.019 --> 00:04:01.841
While Monchi's character, look, and name were
inspired by Monchichi, the equally excitable,

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:04.980
wall-eyed dog of writer-director Mike Rianda's
sister.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:10.239
The zany style of The Mitchells is truly phenomenal
thanks to the animators being encouraged to

00:04:10.239 --> 00:04:13.659
embrace their wildest impulses during production.

00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:18.040
Because most of the movie is told from the
perspective of Katie, who's a filmmaker herself,

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:22.590
the animators created something they called
"Katie Vision" which is where her creativity

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.450
and emotions spill out onto the screen.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.680
The idea was that it should feel as if Katie
edited the movie herself,

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:33.870
so you have 2D doodles and drawings, as well
as internet mashups, memes, and filters popping

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:38.930
up on top of the 3D animation, revealing more
details about Katie's character and feelings

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.100
within a scene.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:44.380
Interestingly, some of the freedom to experiment
on this film came from the success of Spider-Man:

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:49.340
Into The Spider-Verse, as both movies were
produced by Phil Lord and Chris Miller.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:53.810
Because Katie's a filmmaker, almost everything
associated with her is a movie reference or

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:54.810
easter egg.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:59.560
For example, look really carefully at Katie's
socks and you'll see they have the same hexagonal

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:04.620
orange, brown, and red pattern as the iconic
carpet from the Overlook Hotel in The Shining!

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.760
And, in some real attention to detail, those
Shining socks even appear when Katie transforms

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.100
the Columbia Lady logo into her own likeness
at the very start of the film.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:18.420
And while characters from her various home
movies rain down from the sky, the fact that

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:22.700
some of them are food really brings to mind
Cloudy with a Chance of Meatballs, directed

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.500
by Lord and Miller, the producers of this
movie.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.370
The bomb-shaped pin on Katie's hoodie is another
Stanley Kubrick reference, this time to his

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:33.030
1960s Cold War satire Dr Strangelove.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:37.740
And like the bomb in that film, Katie's pin
has the words 'Hi there' written on it.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:42.090
Also on her hoodie are pins of Monchi, the
logo for the California College of Film where

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:46.210
she's been accepted to study, and a rainbow
pin in a bit of foreshadowing to the reveal

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:48.460
of Katie's girlfriend at the end of the movie.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:53.150
And the "Lawn Wranglers" pin on her backpack
is a reference to Wes Anderson's first feature

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:55.460
film, the crime comedy Bottle Rocket.

00:05:55.460 --> 00:06:00.110
Some cool genre movie posters in Katie's room
include horror legend Boris Karloff's Snake

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:04.970
People, the zombie sci-fi "Creature with the
Atom Brain", the monster movie "It Came from

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:07.450
Beneath the Sea", and Robo Slayers 4.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:11.710
And the title seems to be a clever reference
to the Mitchells' own story about a family

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:14.780
of 4 who defeat a robot uprising.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:19.990
The movie's subtitle "Rise of the Brain Exploders"
is also a wink to how the Mitchells use Monchi

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:23.250
to cause the robots to malfunction and self-combust.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:27.680
And another funny detail on the DVD is where
it says it's brought to you by the "visionary

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.210
director of Zombie Flesh Picnic &amp; Werewolf
War Criminal".

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:35.680
For her application to film school, Katie
creates her own personal Mount Rushmore of

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:39.390
Director Heroes
which includes Lady Bird director Greta Gerwig,

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:43.430
French filmmaker Céline Sciamma, Lynne Ramsay
whose most recent feature was You Were Never

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:47.170
Really Here, and Harold and Maude director
Hal Ashby.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:51.050
And there are some neat tributes in Katie's
own assortment of short films to some of those

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.050
directors.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:56.910
So her Portrait Of An Idiot On Fire is a nod
to Sciamma's historical romantic drama Portrait

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:00.760
Of A Lady On Fire;
while Going There references Hal Ashby's Being

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:02.800
There starring Peter Sellers.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:08.310
There's Dial B for Burger, her homage to Alfred
Hitchcock's crime thriller Dial M for Murder,

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:12.920
and two hilarious-looking sequels, Dial B
for Burger 2: Diagnosis which, as we can see

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:17.270
from the injured burger in the thumbnail,
follows up on the events of the first film

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:21.780
where Monchi chomped down on the talking bun:
"Razzle dazzle I'm a talking..

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:22.830
[screaming]
Oh gosh!

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:23.830
Why?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:24.830
Oh, my innards!"

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:29.190
And the final film in the trilogy is Dial
B for Burger 3: Forgiveness where it seems

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:31.860
the burger on his deathbed forgives Monchi.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:36.480
The Perks of Having Only One Friend is a play
on the coming-of-age drama The Perks of Being

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.520
A Wallflower plus Katie's feelings of being
an outsider.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.630
"I've always felt a little different than
everyone else."

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:48.520
While Katie &amp; Aaron is the Mitchell family
spin on the Oscar-winning road movie, Thelma

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.520
&amp; Louise.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:53.790
As for Monchi: Fear Eats The Soul, that's
a riff on the mid-70s film that brought German

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:58.139
filmmaker Rainer Werner Fassbinder his first
international success.

00:07:58.139 --> 00:08:03.900
They Live(D) In The Jurassic Period is a dinosaur-inspired
parody of John Carpenter's 80s movie They

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:07.070
Live where aliens disguised as humans rule
the world.

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:11.200
"I have come here to chew bubble gum and kick
ass.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.570
And I'm all out of bubble gum."

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:18.350
And there's even an amusing riff on that famous
line in one of Katie's Good Cop, Dog Cop films:

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.910
"I'm here to bust criminals and lick my own
butt.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.630
And I'm all out of criminals.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:27.421
And there's also Katie's Director on Director
Q&amp;A which sees her brother kitted out in the

00:08:27.421 --> 00:08:30.300
inimitable style of New Wave director Agnès
Varda.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:33.440
Some other interesting film titles on the
screen are "Oops!

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:37.589
A Wizard Transformed Us Into Chickens", which
seems like it's riffing on "Honey I Shrunk

00:08:37.589 --> 00:08:38.589
The Kids".

00:08:38.589 --> 00:08:44.550
"Chloe, Will You Go To Prom?" might be a video
promposal, another hint to Katie being LGBTQ+.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:49.680
And there's lots more interesting details
in Katie's Good Cop, Dog Cop movies.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:54.089
Her brother who stars as a hardened criminal
drives a car with a perfectly fitting license

00:08:54.089 --> 00:08:55.740
plate CR1MEZ.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:09:00.230
Some cool canine touches in the Dog Cop movie
that Mark watches are a MISSING poster for

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:05.490
a ball, a WANTED poster for a squirrel, a
STOLEN poster for a pair of slippers, and

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:09.420
the motto on the precinct's wall is 'to protect
and serve kibble'.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:13.899
Pictures of other dog favourite objects also
adorn the walls including a fire hydrant and

00:09:13.899 --> 00:09:14.930
a bone.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:19.110
During their time barricaded in the Dino-Stop,
the post-apocalyptic world of the Mad Max

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:23.059
franchise gets a shout-out in Katie's Dope
Plan to defeat the robots.

00:09:23.059 --> 00:09:27.610
"Make a necklace out of robot fingers Mad
Max style, and become world-saving, apocalyptic

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:28.610
road warriors."

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:32.930
When the Mitchells rock up to the Mall of
the Globe, Katie name-checks the second movie

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:36.079
in writer-director George Romero's iconic
zombie film series:

00:09:36.079 --> 00:09:39.100
"This is like Dawn of the Dead."

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.699
"Yeah, and how did that movie end?"

00:09:40.699 --> 00:09:44.740
After the Mitchells lay out their plan to
take down PAL on her home turf then celebrate,

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:49.819
there's a fun scene transition in the style
of the 1960s Batman TV show.

00:09:49.819 --> 00:09:52.040
"Mitchell's engage!"

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:56.089
And as PAL tries to figure out how to stop
the Mitchells, there's a funny freeze-frame

00:09:56.089 --> 00:09:59.800
moment when she orders the robots to pull
up all the family's flaws.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:03.600
An absolute barrage of details pop up on screen,
including:

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.629
"Once brought up his favourite rib during
a eulogy"

00:10:06.629 --> 00:10:11.320
"Looks at ex-boyfriend Carlo Meloni on Facebook
more than is comfortable", which given the

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:16.009
SVU references elsewhere in Katie's films,
makes me wonder if this is a wink to former

00:10:16.009 --> 00:10:19.269
Law &amp; Order: SVU star Christopher Meloni.

00:10:19.269 --> 00:10:23.279
And those family flaws continue with:
"Only pretends to like Fellini"

00:10:23.279 --> 00:10:26.680
"Kicked out of an Olive Garden for stashing
breads in purse"

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:31.300
"Showers with shocking rarity"
"Doctor-diagnosed chocoholic"

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.230
And "Eats own weight in cheese puffs each
month"

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:39.910
And PAL also brings up much more of the Mitchells'
online activity including Aaron's dinosaur-obsessed

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:44.490
search history with him asking questions such
as whether dinosaurs kiss and "how to get

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.839
palaeontologists to reply to your emails".

00:10:46.839 --> 00:10:51.480
Then there's his crush on the girl-next-door
with searches such as "does Abbey Posey have

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:53.730
a boyfriend" and "what is love".

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:59.050
Mum Linda's inbox has revealing email titles
such as "Parent Teacher Night Apology", "'Incident'

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:03.300
with your son", and a "Lifetime Ban" from
what looks like a Best Buy.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:07.070
"It's almost like stealing people's data and
giving it to a hyper-intelligent AI as a part

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:09.790
of an unregulated tech monopoly was a bad
thing."

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:14.951
Of course, despite being what Katie describes
as "the worst family of all time", the Mitchells

00:11:14.951 --> 00:11:18.800
do manage to save the world,
though it's amusing how incredulous the general

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:24.839
reaction is with the cover of People magazine
saying "A nation asks, 'these people, really?'"

00:11:24.839 --> 00:11:27.940
just below their "Family That Saved The World"
headline.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:32.660
On the other hand, the aptly named Poseys
get a much more complimentary write-up on

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.660
the same cover.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:38.940
By the way, given the Poseys' perfect online
family vibe, the filmmakers had some fun casting

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:44.079
model turned TV personality and author Chrissy
Teigen and real-life husband, singer-songwriter

00:11:44.079 --> 00:11:47.699
John Legend, who are also known for their
social media presence.

00:11:47.699 --> 00:11:52.379
While their dino-loving daughter, Abbey, is
voiced by actress, comedian, and writer Charlyne

00:11:52.379 --> 00:11:53.379
Yi.

00:11:53.379 --> 00:11:58.100
Among the stack of films in Katie's home movie
collection is Y tu papá también, a gender-swapped

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:03.320
version of Alfonso Cuarón's hit coming-of-age
film 'Y tu mamá también' which, like The

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.850
Mitchells vs The Machines, is also a road
movie.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:10.380
Crowbar Jones is a hat-tip to the in-universe
film series of the same name that appears

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:13.790
in the Cartoon Network animated show We Bare
Bears.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:18.769
Raptor High is probably a nod to the animated
series Clone High featuring adolescent clones

00:12:18.769 --> 00:12:21.570
of famous historical figures attending high
school.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:25.129
The show was co-created by The Mitchells producers,
Lord and Miller.

00:12:25.129 --> 00:12:30.420
Fists of Furry is an animal-related makeover
of Fists of Fury starring Bruce Lee.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:36.779
And Pugs in Space is a canine take on the
recurring Muppet Show sketch, Pigs In Space.

00:12:36.779 --> 00:12:40.790
Fear And Loathing in Central Michigan is a
reference to Terry Gilliam's Fear And Loathing

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:42.869
in Las Vegas with a nod to Katie's home state.

00:12:42.869 --> 00:12:48.600
Oh, and notice how Katie's DVDs are marked
as the "K Collection", obviously pointing

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:53.749
to her first name's initial, but also a hat-tip
to the Criterion Collection and Kino home

00:12:53.749 --> 00:12:55.779
entertainment labels.

00:12:55.779 --> 00:13:00.639
Given the Mitchells are inspired by co-writer-director
Mike Rianda's own real-life family, it seems

00:13:00.639 --> 00:13:03.079
fitting he voices Katie's younger brother,
Aaron,

00:13:03.079 --> 00:13:04.079
"Hi.

00:13:04.079 --> 00:13:05.680
Would you like to talk to me about dinosaurs?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:06.680
No.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.680
Okay, thank you."

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:10.769
who's loosely based on both Rianda and his
fellow writer-director Jeff Rowe when they

00:13:10.769 --> 00:13:11.769
were kids.

00:13:11.769 --> 00:13:16.670
And Rowe also cameos in the movie as the man
at the Dino Stop who really loves fun.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:17.869
"Who here likes fun?"

00:13:17.869 --> 00:13:19.160
"Hey, I like fun!"

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:21.490
"Trust me, bud, you do not like fun."

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:23.230
"No, I really do like it.

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:24.470
Everyone says that about me."

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:25.790
"You lucky human."

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:30.139
Also at the Dino-Stop, Rowe and Rianda's first
names pop up among the name plate signs in

00:13:30.139 --> 00:13:31.370
the gift shop.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:36.089
Another cameo in The Mitchells is by YouTuber
Elle Mills who voices Hanna, one of Katie's

00:13:36.089 --> 00:13:37.369
film school friends.

00:13:37.369 --> 00:13:38.369
"So good."

00:13:38.369 --> 00:13:43.009
And speaking of Katie's college mates, her
fellow cinephile Dirk Foley is voiced by Alex

00:13:43.009 --> 00:13:47.879
Hirsch who created Gravity Falls, the animated
mystery comedy series which both Mitchells'

00:13:47.879 --> 00:13:51.949
writers and directors Mike Rianda and Jeff
Rowe worked on as well.

00:13:51.949 --> 00:13:52.949
"Mindblowing."

00:13:52.949 --> 00:13:57.629
By the way, Dirk's surname is a filmmaking
in-joke as "foley" is the process of reproducing

00:13:57.629 --> 00:14:01.720
"everyday sound effects" such as footsteps,
opening doors, or breaking glass which are

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:03.699
added into movies during post-production.

00:14:03.699 --> 00:14:09.089
Oh, and Katie's film books also contain a
hat-tip to Dan Hansen, who worked on Disney

00:14:09.089 --> 00:14:13.759
animations including Aladdin and Hercules,
and also taught at CalArts, where this film's

00:14:13.759 --> 00:14:16.970
directors both studied and became friends.

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:21.449
And one of the Mitchells' CG supervisors,
Ben Aguillon, also gets a name-check as writer

00:14:21.449 --> 00:14:25.769
of "Lights, Camera, Angst", suitably enough
as he also supervised the lighting team on

00:14:25.769 --> 00:14:27.489
Spider-Man: Into The Spider-Verse.

00:14:27.489 --> 00:14:33.610
So, I was completely blown away by the animation
and incredible details in The Mitchells vs

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:35.560
The Machines, but what did you notice that
I missed?

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:39.860
Let me know in the comments below and if you
enjoy discovering easter eggs and other hidden

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:44.239
details in animated movies, then tap left
for my full playlist or you can tap right

00:14:44.239 --> 00:14:46.509
to check out something else you're sure to
like.

00:14:46.509 --> 00:14:48.360
Thanks for watching and see ya next time!

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.639
